    "question": {
      ":question/id": "98553e53-de02-548e-9760-3f90719bcb2d",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is a distinct line parallel to $3x-2y=6$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Parallel lines are distinct lines with the same slope. Convert the given line to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3x-2y &=6 \\\\\n-2y &=-3x+6 \\\\\ny &=\\frac{3}{2}x-3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow rewrite each choice:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6x-4y=12 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=\\frac{3}{2}x-3 \\\\\n-6x+4y=8 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=\\frac{3}{2}x+2 \\\\\n3x+2y=6 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-\\frac{3}{2}x+3 \\\\\n2x-3y=6 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=\\frac{2}{3}x-2 \\\\\n6x-2y=6 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=3x-3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equations $6x-4y=12$ and $-6x+4y=8$ both have slope $\\frac{3}{2}$. But $6x-4y=12$ is just twice the original equation: it describes the same line, with the same $y$-intercept of $-3$. It is not a distinct parallel line.\n\nThe equation $-6x+4y=8$ has slope $\\frac{3}{2}$ and $y$-intercept $2$. It describes a different line with the same slope. The other three choices have different slopes.\n\nTherefore, choose $-6x+4y=8$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "bd2e924c-2d5c-51c6-8e95-2f06432bec87",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "6151b5be-99d2-5a19-9d01-2ed08cdc7720",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "6x-4y=12"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "09db3306-4620-58d1-897c-666132452b34",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
